{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Reader-Writer Lock.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Reader-Writer Lock.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"reader writer lock reader writer lock","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Reader-Writer Lock.md","fileName":"Reader-Writer Lock.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Reader-Writer Lock","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 00:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[.NET Synchronization and Thread Coordination]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Synchronization and Thread Coordination","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Reader-Writer Lock.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Reader-Writer Lock.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"reader writer lock reader writer lock","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Reader-Writer Lock.md","fileName":"Reader-Writer Lock.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Reader-Writer Lock","heading":"Reader-Writer Lock","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A reader-writer lock permits several readers to hold the protected resource concurrently while giving a writer exclusive access. It can improve throughput when reads are common, writes are infrequent, and the protected operations are long enough to justify the more complex lock.\n\nUpgrade, recursion, and fairness policies affect contention and starvation. `ReaderWriterLockSlim` reduces overhead for in-process coordination, but an ordinary mutual-exclusion lock is often clearer when the workload does not exhibit genuine read concurrency.","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Synchronization and Thread Coordination","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Reader-Writer Lock.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Reader-W